<DetailLayout
  title="China Trip Builder"
  subtitle="Pick your cities and get a suggested multi-city route with day counts and highlights."
  description="Free interactive China trip planner. Select cities, get a day-by-day route with highlights. Plan your Beijing, Xi'an, Guilin, Shanghai itinerary."
>
  <p class="mb-8 text-stone-600">Design your China itinerary in under a minute. Pick the cities you want to visit in order — we'll suggest how many days to spend in each and what to see. Guilin Yangshuo fits perfectly as the nature segment between urban stops.</p>
  <TripBuilder client:idle />

  <h2>How the Trip Builder Works</h2>
  <h3>Pick Cities, Get a Route</h3>
  <p>Select the cities you want to see and the tool sorts them by flight time, train connections, and season so the route loops instead of crisscrossing the country.</p>
  <h3>Pace Check</h3>
  <p>The day counts flag when your plan is too tight — a common mistake that turns multi-city trips into airport marathons. Slow down one city to see two more properly.</p>

  <h2>Why Guilin Earns Its Days</h2>
  <p>Many itineraries squeeze Guilin into a single day between Guangzhou and Shanghai. That day is worth tripling: the Li River, Yangshuo countryside, and Longji terraces are the landscape most visitors remember from the whole trip.</p>

